keywords:
  - Erdős problems
  - pancyclic graphs
  - extremal graph theory
  - Lean 4
  - GPU search
  - AI agents
abstract: >-
  AI agents determined h(n) = 6 for every 41 <= n <= 67, where m(n) = n + h(n)
  is the minimum number of edges of a pancyclic graph on n vertices
  (Erdős Problem #1016), and showed that the largest n admitting a 6-chord
  pancyclic graph is 67 or lies in {72..79, 81, 83, 84, 85}. Upper bounds are
  kernel-checked in Lean 4; non-existence results are exhaustive computations
  with independently re-derived claim files.
